    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion, mini.snippets\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen inserting a snippet with parameters (LSP or *.json), the indicators will remain onscreen if not filled, causing a layout shift and not being able to be removed until closing and re-opening a file.\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Insert snippet that contains parameters (with mini.completion or mini.snippets)\n2. Go into normal mode\n3. Delete snippet text\n\nBehavior:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d472bd2-1e91-402c-b3cb-06b612218719",
